inciples (control the center early)\n\nReason: Establishing a strong pawn center with d4 is the most solid and ambitious continuation. It gives White maximum control of the center, opens development lines, and follows classical opening principles. The two-pawn center (d4-e4) puts immediate pressure on Black's position and forces them to respond to White's central dominance.\n\nAnswer: P: d2-d4"}
