ze pieces\n- Forces Black to respond defensively\n\nAfter Qh5, Black must deal with the threat to f7. Options like ...Qf6 or ...g6 weaken Black's structure. This keeps Black's king in the center and prevents comfortable development.\n\n**Reason:** Qh5 exploits Black's central king position most effectively, creating immediate tactical threats on f7 and forcing Black into a defensive posture. This prevents Black from consolidating and castling to safety.\n\n**Answer:** Q: d1-h5"}
