ck Queen on c2, forcing it to retreat and relieving immediate pressure on my position. This is the most forcing defensive move, gaining tempo while addressing the primary threat. It's better than passive king moves or rook repositioning that doesn't challenge Black's strongest piece.\n\nAnswer: R: f1-c1"}
